      "title": "Letterboxd review of 50/50",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"50/50\"] My favorite cancer film.It wasn't too light that it can be called shallow. And it wasn't too heavy that it can be called overdramatic.Joseph Gordon-Levitt's character hit the spot where no other 'cancer' film could seem to hit. The rawness of his thoughts cut through the screen and got me thinking and realizing all whilst empathizing. And laughing (thanks, Seth Rogen).This wasn't just a 'cancer' film though-- There was more than the sickness. Real friendships. Clueless newbie counselors. Cheating girlfriends. Awkward blooming connections. Overbearing mothers. Sick fathers. It all perfectly ble",
